local 36-cell stack (GENERATED by gen_rowfields.py; see RECEIPT.md).

From unary inputs `V = |VG|`, `FS = 4s` (writer 9), `NB = nb` (writer 15),
`SL = s*L` (writer 16), `RX = rx` (writer 17), `W29 = binBase`, `W21 =
rawWidth`, `W1 = uniform` it writes, by charged copies, constant writers and
production `multiply_run` products, the words
writer 7 = `V`, writer 18 = `nv = 4s*V`, writers 47..53 (row boundaries and
divisors of `MatrixWeightedEntrySemantic.actualInput`), and the protected
writer's dimension words `rows = 184*rawWidth*binBase*uniform` and
`cols = 2^22*A0*A1*A2*A3`; every scratch cell is then cleared by charged
pops. `rowFields_embedded` runs it inside ANY bank through an injection
(`WeightedRawWords.region_run`, i.e. production `BitMachineStackRun.run`).
`actualD_row_fields` identifies the outputs with the fields of
`ProtectedFullBankBridgeScratch.actualD` and with `actualRows/actualCols`. -/

